% References for open-source-bioreactor
%
% Every literature source docs/references.md rests on, in one file so the whole set can be
% imported into a reference manager at once (Zotero: File > Import, or drag the file in).
% docs/references.md stays the prose record - what each source is used for and where in the
% repo that use lives. This file is the machine-readable half of it and nothing more.
%
% Generated 2026-08-13. The 26 DOI-backed entries are Crossref's own BibTeX, fetched through
% doi.org content negotiation, so the bibliographic fields are the publisher's rather than
% retyped. The 7 entries without a DOI - one thesis, one set of course notes, one conference
% paper, one trade-press article and three patents - are hand-written from the sources.
%
% Each entry's note field carries the two things docs/references.md tracks and BibTeX has no
% field for:
%   Grade                [PR] peer-reviewed - [TH] thesis - [PAT] patent
%                        [TX] textbook - [TP] trade press - [VN] vendor
%   Verification status  read     - full text retrieved, cited passage confirmed
%                        abstract - only the abstract was available
%                        unread   - cited from a secondary source, not obtained
%
% Not included, deliberately: vendor pages, McMaster part numbers and datasheets, and the
% software libraries. Those are cited inline on the registry row or the file that uses them,
% because the row is the thing being justified - see docs/references.md.

